6) Has-A relationship or Association?
   HAS-A relationship represents a relationship where one class contains a reference to an instance of another class.
   It is used to achieve code reusability through composition or aggregation rather than inheritance.
   -->A Has-A relationship represents a relationship between two classes where one class contains a reference to an
      object of another class to use its functionality.

   Note: Easy memory
   IS-A → Inheritance → extends
   HAS-A → Composition/Aggregation → object reference

7) what is composition ?
   Composition is a strong relationship between two classes. If the contained object cannot exist independently without
   the container object, then the relationship is called composition. It represents a strong HAS-A relationship and
   results in tight coupling between the objects.
   Ex:-
   class Engine {
   }

   class Car {
    private Engine engine = new Engine();
   }

8) what is Aggregation ?
   Aggregation is a weak HAS-A relationship between two classes where the contained object can exist independently of
   the container object.

   class Employee {
   }

   class Department {
    private Employee employee;

    Department(Employee employee) {
        this.employee = employee;
    }
   }

